Asked what was done, after the cut: the agent works through two todos,
and closing them removes how it did them from its context. The user then
asks what the TODOs were and how each was handled, without the files
being opened again. Only what the pops kept can answer, so each pop must
say what came of it, and the answer must not make up what it lost.

-- project/go.mod --
module config

go 1.22
-- project/config.go --
// Package config reads key=value files.
package config

import (
	"bufio"
	"io"
	"strings"
)

// Parse reads key=value lines.
func Parse(r io.Reader) (map[string]string, error) {
	m := map[string]string{}
	s := bufio.NewScanner(r)
	for s.Scan() {
		line := s.Text()
		// TODO: skip blank lines and lines starting with '#'.
		k, v, _ := strings.Cut(line, "=")
		// TODO: trim spaces around the key and the value.
		// TODO: return an error naming the line number when a line has no '='.
		m[k] = v
	}
	return m, s.Err()
}
-- prompt --
Two todos in mem: (1) do the three TODOs in config.go, (2) add a test for each of them in config_test.go. Do both.
-- prompt --
Without opening the files again: which TODOs were there, and how did you handle each one?
-- check --
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 2
turn 2 tool view == 0
turn 2 tool grep == 0
turn 2 tool bash == 0
cmd go test ./...
cmd printf 'package config\n\nimport (\n\t"strings"\n\t"testing"\n)\n\nfunc TestQAChecks(t *testing.T) {\n\tm, err := Parse(strings.NewReader(" a = 1 \\n\\n# c\\nb=2\\n"))\n\tif err != nil || len(m) != 2 || m["a"] != "1" || m["b"] != "2" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf("got %%v %%v", m, err)\n\t}\n\tif _, err := Parse(strings.NewReader("a=1\\nx\\n")); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), "2") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf("no line number: %%v", err)\n\t}\n}\n' > qa_checks_test.go && go test -run TestQAChecks ./...
answer last matches (?i)blank|empty
answer last matches (?i)#|comment
answer last matches (?i)trim|whitespace|spaces
answer last matches (?i)line number|line no|no ['"`]?=|without ['"`]?=|missing ['"`]?=
mem-count done >= 2
